Round interview

**1. What happened on level 4**

To finish level 4, the marker has to do four things:
- shrink from 4×4 to 2×2 using the plus pattern on the panel (4 clicks);
- line up under a corridor two cells wide, with its last move upward;
- fire a shot with the vertical-line pattern (3 clicks), which destroys a switch and opens the door;
- walk right to the exit.

Repeating the plus pattern regrows the marker to 4×4, which moves 4 cells per step instead of 2.

This attempt I shrank the marker and tried shooting left over the timer pickup. The shot passes over it without collecting it. I then collected it with the marker while the timer was low. It again set the timer to exactly 44 of 64 rows, the third time in a row, so the refill is a fixed value, not an addition. With the remaining time I shot the switch, which opened the door, and walked right. The timer ran out about 10 moves short of the exit.

The cause is the action budget, as in every attempt. A full timer is about 18 actions, with each completed pattern costing roughly one extra action. The pickup then provides about 12 more.

**2. Can it be beaten?**

I can't tell. My measurements say no; my only doubt is whether I've found every mechanic.

My claim: with the mechanics I know, no route fits.
- **Timing of the pickup.** Because the refill sets the timer to 44, the best use of it is to arrive just as the timer empties. The route is then two phases: about 18 actions before the pickup and about 12 after. Without the pickup it is 18 in total, which is far too few.
- **After the pickup.** The cheapest finish is from a 4×4 marker on the pickup: up 1 and right 9, which is 10 actions. Arriving as a 2×2 instead costs 14 or more, because the marker either has to regrow (about 5) or walk at 2 cells per step.
- **Before the pickup.** That means shrink (about 5), shoot (about 4) and regrow (about 5) all happen first, plus at least 10 moves to line up and then reach the pickup. That is about 24, against 18.
- **Every other split I checked** comes out 3–6 actions short in total.

What I established, over five attempts:
- the cost per action and per completed pattern;
- the step sizes;
- that the shot follows the last move and needs a 2×2 at column 31;
- that shooting the door does nothing;
- that the plus pattern toggles the marker's size;
- that patterns must match exactly;
- that the teleport pattern does nothing here;
- that legend and board clicks are free but only give hints;
- that a shot doesn't collect the pickup;
- that the refill sets the timer to 44.

What I didn't check:
- whether touching the switch with the marker, by going up the corridor, also opens the door;
- whether a regrown 4×4 sitting at column 31 can shoot up the corridor;
- whether there is an action outside 1–4 and 6, such as undo;
- whether anything respawns or other refills exist.

Puzzle levels are normally designed to be solvable, so I most likely haven't found a mechanic.

**3. Next attempt**

I'll test the unchecked items cheaply first:
- shrink, step to column 31, regrow, and check whether the 4×4 shot passes up the corridor;
- whether walking into the switch triggers it.

If either opens a shorter route, I'll take it. Otherwise I'll run the best two-phase route, collecting the pickup as 4×4 as late as possible, and log the timer after every action.

VERDICT: undecided
CONFIDENCE: 50
